    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1602">

                <pb facs="1305" n="1189" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/83.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of Mr.
                    Andrews’s despatch No. 185, of the 10th ultimo, reporting that the special
                    session of the Panaman Assembly adjourned on the 9th ultimo, and that two bills
                    concerning the Panama-David railway had been passed by the Assembly and were
                    then before the President for his approval or veto. Mr. Andrews’s despatch No.
                    190, dated the 16th ultimo, reporting that both bills have been vetoed by the
                    President of Panama,’ has also been received.</p>
                <p>The Department would be glad to have you send it a report, up to date, on the
                    Panama-David Railroad project.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
